jobs.description:
Do you enjoy being active and seeing tangible results? Are you looking for a job where you can work more hours by working at different locations? Then this combined role is perfect for you!
We offer you the opportunity to work at both the Designer Outlet Center in Roermond and De Leistert vacation park in Roggel. By combining these two locations, you can expect a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

What will you be doing?

You’ll be working at two different locations, which ensures plenty of variety in your work:

Designer Outlet Center Roermond

- Cleaning streets and plazas with street sweepers and pressure washers;
- Emptying trash cans on the premises;
- Picking up litter;
- Ensuring a clean and well-maintained environment for visitors.

De Leistert Holiday Park (Roggel)

- Cleaning bungalows, vacation homes, and restroom facilities;
- Making beds;
- Cleaning kitchens, bathrooms, bedrooms, and living rooms;
- Dusting and mopping the accommodations;
- Identifying and reporting any defects.

This combination offers a varied job where you work both indoors and outdoors and see the immediate results of your work.

Work Hours

- Outlet Roermond: flexible availability, including weekends;
- De Leistert: Mondays and Fridays between 9:00 AM and 3:00 PM (alternating days) with the possibility of additional work during the week;
- A combination of both locations allows for a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

- You’re a go-getter and enjoy being active;
- You’re available for at least 15 hours per week;
- You’re flexible (including weekends for the outlet);
- You’re available on Mondays and Fridays (for De Leistert);
- You speak Dutch, English, or German;
- Experience in cleaning is a plus, but not required.

Wat je gaat doen Imagine this: You start your workday together with your colleagues and make sure metal products receive a high-quality finish. Thanks to your attention to detail, products leave the production facility in perfect condition. Experience in powder coating is not required: experienced colleagues will teach you the process step by step. As a powder coating production employee, you are responsible for the final finishing of metal products. Your tasks include:
- Hanging metal products on the powder coating line;
- Removing coated products from the production line;
- Checking products for quality and possible damage;
- Cleaning products, light sanding and performing minor finishing tasks;
- Reporting deviations or quality issues to your supervisor;
- Keeping your workplace clean, organized and safe.

You will work 40 hours per week during the day shift from 07:30 AM to 04:30 PM. This gives you fixed working hours and ensures you are home on time every evening.
   Wat we je bieden - A gross hourly wage starting from €15.02;
- A working week of 24 to 40 hours during the day shift from 07:30 AM to 04:30 PM;
- 25 vacation days based on full-time employment;
- ADV compensation, 8.33% holiday allowance and travel allowance;
- Pension scheme from your first working day;
- An varied position where you can learn a technical profession and continue to develop yourself.

At Start People, we believe in equal pay principles. This means your employment conditions match those of colleagues directly employed by the client, including vacation days, ADV compensation and other employment benefits.
   Functie-eisen For this position, motivation is more important than experience. You enjoy working with your hands and have an eye for quality. In addition:- You are accurate and reliable;
- You do not mind active and standing work;
- You can work independently as well as together with colleagues;
- You understand Dutch, English or German due to work and safety instructions;

SamenvattingReady for the next step in production? Contribute to quality and efficiency! In this role, you are responsible for disassembling, cleaning, testing, and reassembling returned products. This way, you give electronics a second life and directly contribute to a more sustainable process. Do you enjoy varied work and work with precision? Then this is your opportunity!Over de functieYour responsibilities include:
- disassembling returned modems, routers, and parts;
- cleaning components and devices;
- testing individual components and complete products;
- assembling refurbished devices;
- accurately recording test outcomes.

In this company you work from monday to friday, from 07:30 till 16:30.
Over het bedrijfThis company offers comprehensive logistics services with a strong focus on sustainability. They turn returned electronics into valuable refurbished products using high quality and efficient processes.
Wat wij vragen- Energetic and able to stand for 8 hours;
- Interest in electronics and technical tasks;
- Reasonable English language skills;
- Precise, motivated, and team-oriented.

Wat wij bieden- Hourly wage starting from €15.26
- Holiday allowance and vacation hours accrual
- Travel allowance / reimbursement
- High chance of a permanent contract after 6 months
- Realistic opportunities for personal and professional development
- Monthly drinks / social gatherings
- Working in a close-knit and friendly team

Meer informatieWill you start working as a production worker in Bleiswijk? You can apply within just 2 minutes.
Any questions? Thomas will be happy to help you via +31 6 237 235 54 (also WhatsApp) or by email at t.dupuis@carriere.com.
